+{"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"ui","node_id":"U0b","attempt":3,"source":"gate","source_ref":"gate.green t9 at head 8049a28 (docs/trace/ui/U0b/loop.jsonl:24), round A3: the about page has no axe violation; the page shown when trace.json can't be read has no axe violation; the activity page lists every activity line as a row of text","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"A11Y-1","layer":"api","files":["src/web/kit/primitives/status-tag/StatusTag.module.css","src/web/kit/tokens/tokens.css","docs/ui/stylekit/kit.css","docs/ui/styles.md","src/web/app/explorer/about/About.tsx","src/web/app/shell/DataNotice.tsx"],"root_cause":"Layer note: the schema has no web or kit layer. Following the precedent in D1, this is filed as 'api', meaning the web presentation edge. The cause is in the React kit, not the C# API and not the screens. Merge note: this one cause fails two tests, so it is one finding, said openly. The two tests are 'the about page has no axe violation' and 'the page shown when trace.json can't be read has no axe violation'. Symptom: axe reports 'color-contrast (serious)' on exactly one node per page: '.kit-status-tag__fail > span' on #/about and '.kit-status-tag__tag > span' on the unread overview. It does so in the light theme at both 1440 and 390 (src/web/test-results/*/error-context.md). The gate receipt at loop.jsonl:24 names only 'light 1440' and under-reports; the dark theme is clean. Cause: the kit's tag sets its text to the tone colour and its fill to a 10% tint of that same colour (StatusTag.module.css:13-14). The fail tone is --color-error #ca3535 (StatusTag.module.css:24-25, tokens.css:31). Over --color-background #ffffff (tokens.css:24), the fill resolves to about rgb(250,235,235). Relative luminance is 0.154 for the text and 0.856 for the fill, which gives about 4.45:1. That is below AA's 4.5:1 for 14px, weight-600 text (StatusTag.module.css:9-10). The pass tone (#0f7a52, about 4.66:1) and the warn tone (#8a5a00, about 5.15:1) clear the bar, which is why 