+{"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"ui","node_id":"U0b","attempt":2,"source":"david","source_ref":"steer(D1,pause1)","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"RESP-1","layer":"api","files":["src/web/index.html","src/web/app/main.tsx","src/web/kit/layouts/app-shell/AppShell.module.css","src/web/app/shell/App.tsx","src/web/app/shell/NotBuiltPage.tsx"],"root_cause":"Layer note: the schema accepts only domain, services, persistence, api or tests, and has no web layer. This cause is in the web app's screen layer, at the app entry and shell, which is the presentation edge. It is filed as 'api' for that reason only. It is not the C# API and not a tests cause. Symptom: on #/plans/ui/U0b/matrix and #/no-such-page, both of which fall to the catch-all route at src/web/app/shell/App.tsx:17 and render only the short NotBuiltYet box (src/web/app/shell/NotBuiltPage.tsx:7), the footer sits straight under that box and the bare page canvas shows below it. Cause: the shell is built to fill the window and push the footer down. It is a flex column (src/web/kit/layouts/app-shell/AppShell.module.css:6-7), its <main> has `flex: 1 1 auto` (AppShell.module.css:40), and the shell's own height is `min-height: 100%` (AppShell.module.css:12). A percentage min-height needs a parent with a set height, and the app's document gives it none. src/web/index.html:2, :9 and :10 (html, body, #root) carry no height. The only stylesheet src/web/app/main.tsx:8 loads is the kit's tokens.css, which sets only custom properties and color-scheme on :root (src/web/kit/tokens/tokens.css:2-63), with no html, body or #root rule. Repo-wide, the only height rule on that path is AppShell.module.css:12. So the 100% works out to auto, the shell is only as tall as its content, and main's flex-grow has no spare space to fill. The overview, about and activity screens are taller than the window, which hides the defect there. Only short routes show it, and that covers every not-built route. The derived references and the stylekit have the same gap (docs/ui/stylekit/kit.css:4173 `min-height: 100%`, and no html or body rule in docs/ui/stylekit/), so parity checks will not catch it. Interpretation: RESP-1 says the app is 'designed for 1440 and 1280 wide'. The kit's AppShell comment (AppShell.tsx:22-26) describes a page frame of top bar, nav, main and footer. A footer floating mid-window on a laptop-height window breaks that frame. No requirements row names footer placement, so RESP-1 is the closest rule, not an exact one. Fix direction: the page's host document (the app entry, not the kit, which a build node never changes) must give the chain from html through body to #root the window's height, so the kit's percentage min-height has a set parent to resolve against. The body's default margin should go at the same time, so the filled frame fits the window exactly and doesn't scroll by a few pixels. If the orchestrator rules that the kit's own `min-height: 100%` is the defect instead, that is a kit change, to be stopped and reported to David, not patched in a screen.","fingerprint":"RESP-1|src/web/index.html|shell-min-height-percent-of-auto-height-root","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the app served on the complete fixture trail at 1440x900 and at 1280x800, in light and dark, When the page opens #/no-such-page and #/plans/ui/U0b/matrix (both not-built routes, whose content is shorter than the window), Then the footer's box ends within 1px of the window's bottom edge, the document is no taller than the window, and nothing shows below the footer; and on #/ (taller than the window) the footer still follows the content. Tag it 'RESP-1 · on a short page the footer sits at the bottom of the window'. (tests/web/e2e/U0b/resp-1.spec.ts, Playwright)","untestable_reason":null}],"previous_attempts":["attempt 1: gate.red FAIL, the Playwright config failed to load; findings A1; fixed at 380ef5f; gate.red then passed and gate.stub passed at 03ccd8e. A different cause from D1, so no repeated fingerprint."]}
