+fingerprints: ["THEME-1|src/web/index.html|hardcoded-light-first-paint-flips-dark-after-mount-kit-transition", "THEME-1|tests/web/e2e/U0b/theme-1.spec.ts|system-follow-asserts-polled-end-state-only"]
+---
+{"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"ui","node_id":"U0b","attempt":4,"source":"gate","source_ref":"gate.e2e FAIL at t11, docs/trace/ui/U0b/loop.jsonl:54 (head 661cbd8), round A4, with the attempt++ event at loop.jsonl:61. Three full runs of tests/web/e2e/U0b at --workers=1. Run 1 failed 'A11Y-1 · the overview has no axe violation, light and dark, at 1440 and 390'. Run 2 failed 'A11Y-1 · an unbuilt screen's page has no axe violation, light and dark, at 1440 and 390', with color-contrast (serious) in dark at 1440 on .kit-button__button > span and on .kit-theme-toggle__option:nth-child(1..3) > .kit-theme-toggle__face. Run 3 passed 63/63.","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"THEME-1","layer":"api","files":["src/web/index.html","src/web/app/shell/Frame.tsx","src/web/kit/tokens/tokens.css","src/web/kit/primitives/button/Button.module.css","src/web/kit/primitives/theme-toggle/ThemeToggle.module.css","src/web/kit/layouts/top-bar/TopBar.tsx","tests/web/e2e/U0b/a11y-1.spec.ts"],"root_cause":"Layer note: the schema has no web layer, so 'api' stands for the web presentation edge, as in D1, A2 and A3. Symptom: axe, in dark only, intermittently reports color-contrast on the top bar's primary Search button (TopBar.tsx:74-82) and on all three theme-toggle faces (TopBar.tsx:85). It does not hit only one route: run 1 failed the overview, run 2 the unbuilt page. The orchestrator's observation is half confirmed and half disproved. Confirmed: axe measures while the kit's colour transitions are still running. Those are background-color and color over --duration-short, 120ms (tokens.css:19), on the button (Button.module.css:17-19) and the face (ThemeToggle.module.css:57-59). Disproved: the trigger is not page.emulateMedia switching the audited page in place. auditEverywhere sets the colour scheme, then loads about:blank, then loads the route fresh (a11y-1.spec.ts:40-43). The in-place switch at support/app.ts:115 lands only on the page that is about to be thrown away. Cause: the app itself switches theme on every fresh dark-system load. src/web/index.html:2 ships <html data-theme=\"light\">. The token sheet's system-dark rule is scoped to :root:not([data-theme=\"light\"]) (tokens.css:36-37), so that attribute switches it off, and the first paint is always light (tokens.css:22-34), whatever the system says. Only after React has mounted and painted does Frame.tsx:26-31 (useEffect, called at :57) set data-theme to 'dark' (Frame.tsx:29). The top bar's button and toggle are already in the DOM with light computed colours, so that change starts their 120ms fades from the light colours to the dark ones. Halfway through, the text and the fill are both mid-greys, which fails 4.5:1. The audit's readiness checks do not wait for the fades. The unbuilt page's check ('not built yet', a11y-1.spec.ts:72) is met on the first render, and the overview's footer stamp (a11y-1.spec.ts:51) one trace fetch later. So axe sometimes samples inside the 120ms window and sometimes after it. That is why the failure is intermittent, why it moves between routes, and why the overview passed 5/5 alone. The rest is my inference from the timing, not measured. Discriminator: in light, index.html:2 already says 'light' and Frame.tsx:29 writes 'light' again, so nothing changes and nothing fades. Every reported failure is dark, which fits. This breaks THEME-1, 'following the system setting' (docs/ui-requirements.md:184), at first paint, and a real dark-mode user sees a light flash and then a fade. A11Y-1's 'contrast in both themes' (docs/ui-requirements.md:183) fails during that window. The kit is not the cause. Its tokens already follow the system with no attribute (tokens.css:36-49), and its transitions are correct for a change the user makes. kitchen-sink.html:2 carries the same hard-coded light, but that is kit-owned and outside U0b. Evidence gap: run 1's axe message is not in the receipt (loop.jsonl:54 names the test only), and src/web/test-results/ holds only .last-run.json. That run 1 had the same cause is inferred from the same top bar being on every route, not proven. Why the earlier route didn't prevent it: this is the first fingerprint, with no match in A1, D1, A2 or A3. The web-tester saw a theme-toggle__face flag once at the A3 finding-red (its greps at activity.jsonl:804-807) but never filed it, and the six clean repeats were read as clearance. Repeats cannot clear a timing race. It probably became more frequent because of I3's fix. A2 I3 records that the old Frame.tsx swapped in an UnreadFrame, with no kit top bar, while the trace loaded. The top bar therefore mounted only after the theme had already switched, and inherited dark with no fade. The current Frame.tsx:94-98 renders the kit AppShell from the first commit, so the top bar now fades on every dark load. I took the old code from A2's description, not from that commit. Fix direction: on a fresh load the document must not declare a theme the system contradicts. The first paint must already follow the system setting, so applying the choice after mount changes no colour on a normal load and starts no fade. The CSP (index.html:6, default-src 'self') rules out an inline pre-paint script. The test must not be bent to hide this: no reduced-motion emulation, and no waiting out the fades as the only change. Owner: web-builder (src/web/index.html and src/web/app/shell/Frame.tsx). No /kit-gap is needed.","fingerprint":"THEME-1|src/web/index.html|hardcoded-light-first-paint-flips-dark-after-mount-kit-transition","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the system emulated as dark before navigation, and an init script that records, from the moment the parser creates <html>, every value its data-theme attribute takes until the page is ready, When the overview opens on the complete fixture trail and its footer stamp shows, Then the recorded values never include 'light' and the last is 'dark'. (A new 'THEME-1 · on a fresh load the first theme the page shows follows the system setting, dark' in tests/web/e2e/U0b/theme-1.spec.ts, added in its own red commit by the web-tester. It is deterministic, not a race: index.html:2 parses with 'light' before any script runs, on every load. It turns green only when the first paint follows the system. Afterwards the existing A11Y-1 axe tests should pass on repeat, e.g. --repeat-each 10 at --workers=1, as supporting evidence only.)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I2","rule_id":"THEME-1","layer":"tests","files":["tests/web/e2e/U0b/theme-1.spec.ts","tests/web/e2e/U0b/support/app.ts","tests/web/e2e/U0b/a11y-1.spec.ts"],"root_cause":"Same symptom as I1, different cause, filed separately and said openly. I1 is why the page is wrong. I2 is why no test catches it every time, so the suite reports it as a flake rather than a red. (a) 'THEME-1 · with no choice made, the theme follows the system setting' (theme-1.spec.ts:18-26) checks only the end state. toHaveAttribute('data-theme','dark') at :25 retries until it holds, so it passes after the late switch and never sees the light first paint. (b) The audit's 'tokens are in force' check (a11y-1.spec.ts:45) reads the --color-background custom property (support/app.ts:123-131). A custom property changes the instant data-theme does and is never animated, so the check passes while the button and toggle colours are still fading. It cannot detect the state axe is measuring. The only signal left is axe's timing, which is why the A3 sighting (activity.jsonl:804-807) was cleared by repeats instead of turning red. First occurrence, so it has no prior fingerprint. Fix direction: the THEME-1 suite needs a check that sees the page's first theme, not only its final one (the red in I1). The existing A11Y-1 audits stay as they are. Making them stable by emulating reduced motion (tokens.css:64-66 sets --duration-short to 0), or by waiting out the fades without the new red, would hide the defect: that would weaken them after their red commit. Owner: web-tester.","fingerprint":"THEME-1|tests/web/e2e/U0b/theme-1.spec.ts|system-follow-asserts-polled-end-state-only","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the system emulated as dark before navigation and the <html> data-theme recorded from document creation, When the overview opens and is ready, Then 'light' was never recorded. (The same new red as I1, in tests/web/e2e/U0b/theme-1.spec.ts. One test closes both the app cause and this test gap; it is named here so the gap is not lost.)","untestable_reason":null}],"previous_attempts":["attempt 1: gate.red FAIL, the Playwright config failed to load; A1 (DATA-1|src/web/tsconfig.json|paths-wildcard-routes-playwright-to-cjs-index, DATA-1|src/web/package.json|types-node-resolved-outside-repo); unrelated.","attempt 2: David's steer D1 at pause 1 (RESP-1|src/web/index.html|shell-min-height-percent-of-auto-height-root), fixed at 98b45f4. It touches the same file as I1, but at a different line and with a different cause (the height chain, not data-theme), so it is not a repeat.","attempt 2: t9 gate.green FAIL 59/62; attempt 3; inv-004 issued A2 (four fingerprints: StatusTag tint contrast, header innerText, UnreadFrame skip link, cssMinify string compare), all accepted; KG2, KG3, tester corrections and builder fix; t9 green 63/63; none matches I1 or I2.","attempt 3: at the A3 finding-red the web-tester saw a theme-toggle__face contrast flag once (activity.jsonl:804-807), it did not recur in six repeats, and it was never filed. That is the same cause as I1, first seen but not fingerprinted. I3's fix (the kit AppShell in every trace state) probably widened the window by mounting the top bar before the theme switch (inferred from A2 I3's account of the old code).","attempt 3: t11 first run failed audit and coverage (harness, fixed by #65, no attempt by David's ruling); the re-run on #65 failed gate.e2e intermittently (loop.jsonl:54), so attempt 4. I1 and I2 are first fingerprints and do not escalate the retry ladder."]}
