+---
+plan_id: inv-005
+kind: investigation
+title: U0b review fails on the compiler's missing attempt and unscanned git values
+created: 2026-10-21
+dag: null
+parent: ui/U0b
+---
+# inv-005: U0b review fails on the compiler's missing attempt and unscanned git values
+## Question
+Why does the reviewer FAIL ui/U0b at attempt 4 on HONEST-1 and DATA-5, and is the cause in the compiler code, in the tests, or in both?
+## Hypothesis
+The compiler's activity chunk and commit output were written to the field lists the t5 unit tests named, so code and tests share the same omissions (attempt; trailer values and compiledAt.ref), and the Playwright activity read-back skips Attempt for the same reason. Disproved if any test at HEAD asserts attempt in the activity chunk or on the page, or plants a denylisted trailer value, and still passes against the current compiler.
+## Evidence
+- docs/trace/ui/U0b/verdicts/A4-reviewer.json: FAIL, P1 R1-R3 (HONEST-1, DATA-5), P2 R4-R5 (DATA-1)
+- docs/trace/ui/U0b/verdicts/A4-security.json: PASS; P2 S2 is R3's cause, S1 and S3 are hygiene
+- docs/trace/ui/U0b/findings/A4.md: the investigator's diagnosis, I1-I6
+- docs/trace/ui/U0b/packet/: the reviewed diff, trailers and gates at 690ad15
+- docs/trace/ui/U0b/loop.jsonl:78-82: the verdicts, attempt 4 → 5 and this investigation
+## Findings
+Both. The cause sits in the compiler and in the tests together, and no test at HEAD names attempt or plants a value from git outside the commit subject, so the hypothesis holds. One part does not: the compiler's field list is not copied from the tests (it emits line, ts and commit, which they don't name), but both leave out the same fields. See [findings/A4.md](../../trace/ui/U0b/findings/A4.md).
+- I1 (new, HONEST-1, blocking): the activity chunk is built from a fixed field list without attempt (src/web/compiler/index.ts:149), so every Attempt cell shows a dash the trail contradicts.
+- I2 (new, HONEST-1, blocking): the tests' ActivityLine has no attempt (tests/web/unit/compiler/support/trail.ts:51-56, tests/web/e2e/U0b/support/trail.ts:145-150), so the chunk test (data-1.test.ts:103) and the read-back (a11y-1.spec.ts:171-179) never see I1. inv-004's A2/I2 test listed the same columns.
+- I3 (new, DATA-5, blocking): the denylist scans the compiler's inputs and the commit subject only (index.ts:88-93, :111); trailer values (:112-124) and compiledAt.ref (:206) are written unscanned. It is security's S2 too.
+- I4 (new, DATA-5, blocking): the only test with a value from git plants it in the subject (data-5.test.ts:93-108), while its header claims every emitted value.
+- I5 (new, DATA-1, non-blocking): trailersOf keeps only the last value of a repeated key (src/web/compiler/git.ts:40), so commits with several Fixes-Finding lines lose all but one; no U0b screen reads it, U3 is the first reader.
+- I6 (new, DATA-1, non-blocking): events, verdicts and rules[].status/red/green are filled by parsers no red test drives (index.ts:154-200); no U0b screen reads them.
+## Recommendations
+```yaml recommendations
+- {kind: amend-node, target: ui/U0b, rule: HONEST-1, reason: "I1+I2: web-tester red first: give both ActivityLine types every field the screen reads, add attempt to the chunk-shape test, and a HONEST-1 e2e reading every activity column (Attempt '1' on rows 1-5) against the fixture; then the web-builder carries attempt into the chunk", status: proposed}
+- {kind: amend-node, target: ui/U0b, rule: DATA-5, reason: "I3+I4: web-tester red first: a denylisted Rule trailer and a denylisted --ref each fail the compile without printing the match, and the test header claims only what it proves; then the web-builder scans every emitted value from git (or the serialised output) before writing", status: proposed}
+- {kind: amend-node, target: ui/U0b, rule: DATA-1, reason: "I6: the compiler emits empty events and verdicts and no derived rule status/red/green, with a red test asserting the empty lists, until U1 (rule status) and U3 (events, verdicts) drive them with their own reds", status: proposed}
+- {kind: feature, target: null, reason: "David's ask: a final tech-debt node at the end of ui.dag.yaml for non-blocking carries: security S1 (rel=noreferrer) and S3 (CSP base-uri/form-action/object-src), I5 if U3 has not landed it, and any non-blocking P2 a later review raises", status: proposed}
+```
+## Why
+U0b's attempt-4 review (the node's first reviewer round) FAILed, which made attempt 5, the retry ladder's stop. David chose to investigate rather than cut or take over: "lets work on these plan investigation - and if it fails again perhabs we can add a final node to the plan-dag for tech debt that we can carry if its not blocking".
+## Approach
+Read-only: the A4 verdicts and packet, the earlier findings and inv-004, and the investigator's diagnosis (findings/A4.md). The 30m time box held. The route at attempt 5 runs the tester reds (I2, I4, I6) before the builder fixes (I1, I3, I6). attempt is capped at 5, so a further FAIL goes to David: its non-blocking findings to the tech-debt node, blocking ones for his ruling.
+## Rejected alternatives
+- Fix the screen to hide the Attempt column, or reword the dash: the trail has the value, so hiding it loses evidence the signed-off contract shows.
+- Keep the I6 parsers and test them all in U0b: it pulls U1's and U3's compiler work into a node already at attempt 5; emptying the lists costs less and makes no claim.
+- Fix I5 now: no U0b screen reads fixesFinding, and the fixture format can't express a repeated trailer yet; it belongs with U3's compiler red, its first reader.
+- Fix S1 and S3 now: P2 hygiene that doesn't fail the review; carried to the tech-debt node so none is lost.
+## Prior work consulted
+- docs/plans/active/inv-004.plan.md: the attempt-3 investigation of U0b; its A2/I2 corrected the activity read-back's headers without Attempt
+- docs/plans/active/ui.dag.yaml:43-72: U0b's rules and tasks (DATA-5 acceptance: fails on a privacy-denylist match)
+- docs/lessons.md: none
+## Attempt log
