 {"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"ui","node_id":"U0b","attempt":5,"source":"reviewer","source_ref":"docs/trace/ui/U0b/verdicts/A4-reviewer.json R1, R2, R3, R4, R5 (round A4, loop.jsonl:78-79); R3 overlaps docs/trace/ui/U0b/verdicts/A4-security.json S2 (PASS verdict, P2)","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"HONEST-1","layer":"api","files":["src/web/compiler/index.ts","src/web/app/explorer/activity/Activity.tsx","src/web/app/data/trace.ts","tests/web/fixtures/trails/complete/trail/docs/trace/build/F1/activity.jsonl","docs/ui/derived/U0b/activity/screen.json"],"root_cause":"Layer note: the schema has no web layer, so 'api' stands for the web app here, as in D1, A2 and A3. This cause is in the build-time trail compiler. Symptom (R1): on the activity page every Attempt cell shows a dash, and Activity.tsx:106-108 tells the reader that a dash means the log holds no value for that column. Cause: the compiler builds each activity line from a fixed list of fields at src/web/compiler/index.ts:149: line, ts, agent, tool, file, command and commit. attempt is not on that list, so it is dropped even though every source line has it. The complete fixture carries attempt 1 on lines 1-5 (activity.jsonl:1-5). The live trail has 1092 attempt values in docs/trace/ui/U0b/activity.jsonl. The signed-off contract names activity.json[].attempt (docs/ui/derived/U0b/activity/screen.json:17, :26). The screen and the loader are not the cause. Activity.tsx:46 correctly falls back to the dash when attempt is missing, and the loader passes the chunk through unchanged (trace.ts:136). Its type marks attempt as optional (trace.ts:65), so nothing at compile time notices it is gone. The page therefore shows an absence that the trail contradicts. HONEST-1 (docs/ui-requirements.md:187) says no build may show a number, status or name that isn't in the trail, and a false 'none' is such a claim. Hypothesis check: partly right. The compiler's field list is not copied from the test's list, because the compiler also