ds it. The cost of carrying it: trace.json misstates this trail until then, which no screen shows.","fingerprint":"DATA-1|src/web/compiler/git.ts|trailers-fromentries-keeps-last-of-repeated-key","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given a fixture repo with a commit carrying two trailer lines, 'Fixes-Finding: A1/I1' and 'Fixes-Finding: A1/I2', When the compiler runs, Then that commit's fixesFinding is [{round 1, id I1}, {round 1, id I2}] in that order. (tests/web/unit/compiler, U3's compiler red)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I6","rule_id":"DATA-1","layer":"api","files":["src/web/compiler/index.ts","tests/web/unit/compiler/data-1.test.ts"],"root_cause":"Layer note: 'api' stands for the web app's build-time compiler. Symptom (R5): trace.json's events, verdicts and rules[].status/feature/red/green are filled by logic that no test drives and no U0b screen reads. Cause: during U0b's green step the web-builder wrote parsers that go beyond the node's red tests: loop.jsonl events (index.ts:154-163), verdict envelopes and rounds (:164-179), and a rule status derived from TDD trailers (:189-200). A search of tests/web/unit and tests/web/e2e for events, verdicts, rulesCovered, 'built', .red, .green or fixesFinding finds nothing. The only DATA-1 checks are the index's field list (data-1.test.ts:45-49), rule ids (:60) and commit fields (:63-82). No U0b screen reads these values: src/web/app reads only nodes, commits and the activity chunk. web-testing says each behaviour follows its red. A status of 'built' derived without a test is also a claim waiting to reach a screen. When U1 shows rule status, a wrong value there would breach HONEST-1, and today nothing would catch it. First occurrence. Fix direction: either drive each parser with red tests on the fixture trails (fail-and-fix holds the loop events and both verdict rounds) or emit empty lists until the nodes that own them drive them. The schema needs the lists to exist, not to be filled. David chooses which. Blocking for U