uild/F1/activity.jsonl","docs/trace/ui/U0b/findings/A2.md"],"root_cause":"Recurrence: this is the A4/I2 cause, still unfixed. The tests at HEAD are the reviewed ones. Separate cause from I1, said openly: I1 is why the page is wrong, and I2 is why the suite passed 64/64 anyway (loop.jsonl:71). Symptom (R2): no test reads the Attempt column. Cause: the tests' own description of an activity line has no attempt field. ActivityLine is {agent, tool, command, file} in both tests/web/unit/compiler/support/trail.ts:51-56 and tests/web/e2e/U0b/support/trail.ts:145-150. The chunk test maps exactly those four fields (tests/web/unit/compiler/data-1.test.ts:103). The page read-back checks Line, Agent, Tool, File or command, Commit and TDD, skips Attempt (tests/web/e2e/U0b/a11y-1.spec.ts:173-178), and is tagged A11Y-1. No HONEST-1 test compares a cell's value with the trail: honest-1.spec.ts:55-79 checks only the heading, placeholders and foreign ids. Why the previous route didn't prevent it: A2/I2 (inv-004) fixed this read-back's header lookup, and its suggested test (docs/trace/ui/U0b/findings/A2.md:18) listed the columns without Attempt, so the green it produced looked complete. Its fingerprint differs (header case), so it is not a repeat of that cause. Fix direction (accepted reason 1, red first): give both ActivityLine types every field the chunk carries and the screen reads: line, ts, attempt, agent, tool, file, command, commit {sha, subject} and raw, but not commit.tdd (see I1). Add a HONEST-1 e2e that reads every column of rows 1-5 against the complete fixture, Attempt included. Adding Attempt to the A11Y-1 read-back at a11y-1.spec.ts:171-179 strengthens it and weakens nothing. Not a source for attempt in this route: the fail-and-fix fixture contradicts itself. Its activity.jsonl:6-8 (commits c5-c7, made after attempt++ at its loop.jsonl:8) hold attempt 1 and times 13:05-13:07, which fall before the 16:00 verdict at loop.jsonl:6, while its loop.jsonl:8-14 hold attempt 2. No test under tests/web names that fixture today. This is a note for the tech-debt node or U3, not a finding for U0b.","fingerprint":"HONEST-1|tests/web/e2e/U0b/a11y-1.spec.ts|activity-readback-and-chunk-shape-omit-attempt","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the complete fixture trail compiled and served, and #/plans/build/F1/activity open, When rows 1-5 of the event table are read, Then each row's Attempt cell reads '1' (not the dash), and Line, Agent, Tool, File or command, Commit and TDD trailer read the values the fixture's activity.jsonl and commits.json hold. (tests/web/e2e/U0b/honest-1.spec.ts: 'HONEST-1 · the activity page shows every column of each line as the trail holds it'. Red at HEAD on the Attempt cell, because index.ts:149 drops attempt.)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I3","rule_id":"DATA-5","layer":"api","files":["src/web/compiler/index.ts","src/web/compiler/privacy.ts","docs/trace/privacy-denylist.txt",".githooks/commit-msg"],"root_cause":"Recurrence: this is the A4/I3 cause, still unfixed. index.ts at HEAD is the reviewed file. Merge note, kept from A4: R3 and security's S2 have one cause, so they are filed once. Layer note: 'api' stands for the build-time compiler. Symptom: commit trailer values and compiledAt.ref reach trace.json without the denylist. Cause: the scan is attached to inputs. read() scans every docs file it reads (index.ts:88-93), and one extra scan covers the commit subject (:111). The trailer values emitted at :112-124 and the ref emitted at :206 pass no scan, and the compile fails only on what was scanned (:202). Rule: DATA-5 (docs/ui-requirements.md:112), 'The compiler fails the build if its output matches the privacy denylist'. The commit-msg hook does not close the gap. It runs only on feature/*/* and bug/*/* branches (.githooks/commit-msg:6-9), so a commit made on main carries unchecked trailers, and even on those branches Rule is checked only for being non-empty (:35). New in this diagnosis, three points the builder 